      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/a/59ef9b/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2015-04-10T04:03:24.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>We came to a different conclusion in my play group.&nbsp; We took the sentence \"I<span>f there are no Room cards in play, reshuffle this card into the Environment deck and play the top card of the Environment deck.\"</span> to be a constant effect, which took effect when the Room was destroyed.&nbsp; (When the question came up, the Entry-Pointed Rooom was the only one in play.&nbsp; Considering the case of multiple Rooms in play makes me more dubious about that conclusion...)</p>",
