      "user_title": null,
      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>We came to a different conclusion in my play group.&nbsp; We took the sentence &quot;I<span style=\"font-size:110.0%;font-family:calibri,arial,sans,sans-serif;color:#000000;text-align:left;\">f there are no Room cards in play, reshuffle this card into the Environment deck and play the top card of the Environment deck.&quot;</span> to be a constant effect, which took effect when the Room was destroyed.&nbsp; (When the question came up, the Entry-Pointed Rooom was the only one in play.&nbsp; Considering the case of multiple Rooms in play makes me more dubious about that conclusion...)</p>",
