      "raw": "[quote=\"AlexxKay\"]\n\nWe came to a different conclusion in my play group.&nbsp; We took the sentence &quot;If there are no Room cards in play, reshuffle this card into the Environment deck and play the top card of the Environment deck.&quot; to be a constant effect, which took effect when the Room was destroyed.&nbsp; (When the question came up, the Entry-Pointed Rooom was the only one in play.&nbsp; Considering the case of multiple Rooms in play makes me more dubious about that conclusion...)\n\n[/quote]\n\nThe sentence is not a seperate constant effect. It is a conditional part of the &quot;Play this on a room&quot; action, because there nessesarily needs to be instructions of how you play that card &quot;on a room&quot; when there are no room cards.\n",
