      "raw": "[quote=\"Ameena\"]\n\nIsn&#39;t the Room card (the one covered by the Entry Point) considered to basically not exist whilst covered? Or is it just that it has no text (and could thus presumably still be destroyed by &quot;Destroy an environment card&quot; effects)? I&#39;ve not played in the Freedom Tower for a while so I can&#39;t remember.\n\n[/quote]\n\nThe room that is covered is still\n\nfrom the deck which we call &#39;vironmental\n\nBut is it still a room?\n\nThough the text was consumed\n\nSo one room can be home to them all?\n\n&nbsp;\n\nEntry Point removes the &quot;game text&quot; of the card. &nbsp;As was addressed in a different thread, when Guise&#39;s Uh, Yeah, I&#39;m that Guy refers to game text, it is only referring to the text box, and doesn&#39;t refer to the type line. &nbsp;By this logic, the room under Entry Point would still be a room, and multiple Entry Points could be played on one room. &nbsp;Of course, generally cards under other cards are considered to have no text or types. &nbsp;I suspect that this is the case here, in which case I think the wording of the card is ambigous.\n\nRegardless, the room card is still an environment card, and would be destructible by environment destruction.\n",
