      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"MigrantP\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/migrantp/48/1921_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MigrantP:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Self-Destruct Countdown + Dominion + Terraforming = extra card draws, if you're careful!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>And this could go bad if you're wrong</p>\n<p>and misorder the death of the throng</p>\n<p>if you let the countdown go last</p>\n<p>then your hope will be past</p>\n<p>and the game will be over ere long</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Basically, you can destroy the cards under Self-Destruct Countdown before you destroy the countdown itself, but if you do then you will lose when the countdown notices that it's pile is empty and blows up.</p>\n<p>It's even worse if you're destroying the environment using Terraforming, because even if you don't blow up (say you noticed at the last second, and destroyed the countdown before its last card), then Omnitron will play a card for every card it destroyed. &nbsp;If you destroy the countdown first then it's not a problem because it wasn't terraforming that destroyed the other cards, it was the countdown. &nbsp;But if you go the other way, then watch out!</p>",
